{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00634 - MONDO_2970",
  "verbalization": "Sulfacetamide is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ciliary Body Disease through a series of indirect pathways involving uveitis and fluorometholone or medrysone. The drug's indication for Uveitis, which in turn is linked to Fluorometholone or Medrysone, both of which are indicated for Ciliary Body Disease, suggests a potential mechanism by which Sulfacetamide may influence ciliary body function. The cumulative evidence points to a possible role of Sulfacetamide in triggering uveitis, which could then lead to the development of Ciliary Body Disease via the actions of its metabolites. The strength of the evidence is supported by the overlapping indications across different paths, indicating a plausible but not definitively established relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of uveitis as a potential mediator in the link between Sulfacetamide and Ciliary Body Disease.",
